# PHASE 2 of a grasp. Needs a verified pre-grasp. Remove the target from the
# collision scene, move straight in, check the open jaws straddle the object,
# close, attach it and lift straight up.
#
# `plan` is the CURRENT best plan: if the object's dimensions were refined since
# the pre-grasp, its grasp_point.z may differ and the straight-in move ends at
# the corrected height. Its x, y must match the pre-grasp's (within 2 cm).
GraspPlan plan
geometry_msgs/Point object_now  # object position now (the camera is occluded here)
bool object_now_valid           # false = unknown; the contact check then passes
---
bool success
bool verified                   # contact check passed (false = jaws not centred; did not close)
bool descended                  # the jaws moved in around the object
bool straddled
float64 along_jaw               # m, object offset along the closing axis; NaN = not measured
float64 in_plane_miss           # m, offset along the approach axis; NaN = not measured
float64 gripper_width           # measured left_finger position after the attempt (m)
string message
